 "note": "Rig v2 with smooth joints (2026-11-11): standard biped skeleton (docs/puppet-kit-next.md section 3). Each limb and the torso is ONE picture bent around its joints (\"skin\": the pixels near a joint turn by a fraction of the joint angle), so a bent elbow, knee or waist is a curve, not a cut. The cut version is rig_v2_cut.json, the first rig rig_v1.json. Layers come from stills erased from the master with the head kept as an anchor. Legs: two-bone IK to a planted foot. Pixels of the 1024x1024 stills; unit = standing silhouette = 2 x {H} at @2x. Studio v01 (2026-11-11): added near_foot_target / far_foot_target (children of root, at each IK target) so the pose can move each foot with tx/ty; at rest the result is identical to rig.json. Limits and links added by the Studio (docs/puppet-studio.md): bone.limit.rot = allowed rot range, links = muscle links (the shoulder slides out and the chest near each anchor follows).",
